TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
  vertices=sidecar repairs over the coarse actual-packet sheaf base
  pairwise_observable=number of mixed theorem-exit fibers surviving on enlarged banks
  priority_path=residue_plus_owner_support -> residue_plus_unit_qsqrt7 -> residue_plus_v2 -> residue_plus_height -> residue_plus_unit_slot -> residue_only
  directed_3cycles=0
  hamiltonian_path_count=1

CONCLUSION
  The nonunit residue word is only a curated-bank separator.
  On the expanded HYP-2963 banks, the first leak is height-driven
    (P10+GW vs GW-shell alias 12->132),
  but the stronger leak is endpoint-owner-driven
    (petal 13->26 vs the positive-open single-swap 26-family).
  Exact readout through single_limit=60 and two_swap_limit=16:
    residue+v2 and residue+exact_height still leave mixed theorem-exit fibers,
    while residue+owner_support kills all mixed kernel fibers.
  So HYP-3402's endpoint-owner current route is the next exact repair
  on the enlarged bank; tropical height data explains only the first subcase.
